# internal/adapter is the one package whose floor is set below the current measurement on purpose.
# Its coverage moves with which S3-backed tests the harness can run, and the write-path rebuild
# will churn it substantially; 40 is the level below which it has genuinely regressed.
internal/adapter         40

# internal/fuse is lowered from 24 to 17 by the write-path rebuild, and this is the one shape of
# lowering that is not a weakened gate: the drop is the deletion of tests for deleted code. The
# WriteCoalescer and its thirteen tests are gone — the type corrupted data on a routine overwrite
# while every one of those tests passed — so the numerator and the denominator both fell, and the
# statements that remain are covered exactly as well as they were before.
#
# 17 is not a target. This package is a 727-line coupling of POSIX semantics to go-fuse types with
# no seam to test at, which is what task #22 is for: once it is a translation shim over
# internal/vfs (98%), its floor goes up with the rewrite rather than ahead of it.
internal/fuse            17

